description.narrative:
The Investment Council of Armenia will continue to work on improving the investment climate in 2026 – 2028, including through its assistance to the Deputy Prime Minister led private-public dialogue Council, Ministry of Economy and Deputy Prime Minister Office. Priority areas will include:    
1. Trade diversification; 
2. Access to finance for SMEs;  
3. Improvements to the investment climate in Armenia; 
4. Promotion of innovation and entrepreneurship 
5. Regional inclusivity and growth 
6. Digitization of the administrative processes 
Armenia works closely within the trilateral support mechanism: the Private Sector, the Government, and the donor community. Over the course of the period, the Secretariat will explore opportunities to ensure the sustainability of the IC Armenia operations through securing the contributions of the three above-mentioned actors in the period after March 2027. Particularly, the private sector will contribute financially to hold the outreach events that IC Armenia implements, as well as pro bono tax consultants, whereas the Government will contribute with hall rentals and work with local authorities. Secretariat’s staff will need to continue to be covered through any donor funding, which will allow to ensure the long-term credibility, impartiality, and functional capacity of IC Armenia. As a convening platform for multiple stakeholders, it is essential that the impartiality of Secretariat’s analytical and advisory work is maintained.
